  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political alliance between the Congress and the Samajwadi Party in Uttar Pradesh is currently facing significant strain, leading to an indefinite pause in seat-sharing discussions. Observers note that no further formal negotiations are anticipated until the current parliamentary session concludes in early December. The deadlock follows public criticism from Congress members regarding the alliance's conditions, prompting intervention from national leadership to manage internal conduct. Concurrently, the Samajwadi Party has moved forward by unveiling its election manifesto. The policy document emphasizes economic and social initiatives, including promises of 2.5 million government jobs, monthly stipends for unemployed graduates, immediate debt relief for farmers, and the provision of 300 units of free electricity. These developments reflect broader challenges in coordinating electoral strategy between the two parties as they prepare for the upcoming state assembly elections.",
